<speak>
<s>From <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="zʊhd">zuhd</phoneme> news, this is your briefing for <say-as interpret-as="date" format="dmy">22022026</say-as>.</s>
<s>It's ten past seven in the evening in <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="ˈmæk.kæ">Makkah</phoneme>.</s>
<break time="1s"/>
<s>Iran has hardened its nuclear installations at <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="nɑːˈtɑːnz">Natanz</phoneme> and placed a senior military commander in charge of war contingency planning, even as Tehran and Washington agreed to resume nuclear talks in early March.</s>
<s>Satellite images revealed reinforced tunnel entrances at the site, and American strike forces are expected in position by mid-March.</s>
<s>Tehran is demanding the lifting of all sanctions; Washington has offered only partial relief, and the gap between them remains wide.</s>
<break time="900ms"/>
<s>In politics.</s>
<break time="400ms"/>
<s>Israeli settlers seized five Palestinian-owned buildings in a densely populated neighborhood of Hebron, declaring a new settlement without government approval, after soldiers arrested dozens of Palestinian residents.</s>
<s>The settlers vowed not to wait for official sanction, deepening a pattern of land seizure in a city already divided by a decades-old agreement.</s>
<s>Whether the action is lawful under either Israeli or international law remains unresolved.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>The unrecognized territory of Somaliland has offered the United States mineral rights and a Red Sea military base in exchange for diplomatic recognition.</s>
<s>Somaliland's foreign minister said the offer includes lithium and coltan, minerals critical to battery and electronics manufacturing.</s>
<s>Washington has not formally responded, though President Trump indicated last August he was considering the matter.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Brazil's President Lula challenged Washington to apply tariffs equally to all nations, speaking from New Delhi where he signed critical minerals agreements with Prime Minister Modi to diversify trade.</s>
<s>The deals come as forty percent American tariffs on Brazilian exports remain in force.</s>
<s>Lula travels to Washington to meet President Trump next month.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>The Australian frigate HMAS <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="tuːˈwʊmbə">Toowoomba</phoneme> completed a transit of the Taiwan Strait on Friday, with China's navy shadowing it throughout the passage.</s>
<s>Canberra said all interactions were safe; Beijing has long claimed the strait as Chinese internal waters, a position Western nations dispute.</s>
<s>At least three allied nations have made similar transits this year.</s>
<break time="900ms"/>
<s>In conflict and security.</s>
<break time="400ms"/>
<s>Russia fired dozens of ballistic missiles and drones at Kyiv before dawn Saturday, striking homes across five districts two days before the invasion's fourth anniversary.</s>
<s>In Lviv, a decoy emergency call lured police to a bomb that killed a twenty-three-year-old officer and wounded fifteen others, hundreds of kilometres from the front lines.</s>
<s>The war enters its fifth year on Monday with no ceasefire in sight.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Pakistani airstrikes hit Taliban camps in the Afghan provinces of <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="ˌnæŋɡɑːˈhɑːr">Nangarhar</phoneme> and <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="pækˈtiːkə">Paktika</phoneme>, with Kabul reporting dozens killed, among them civilians and children.</s>
<s>Afghanistan's Taliban administration said the strikes destroyed a school and homes.</s>
<s>Kabul has promised a measured response but warned the attacks threaten the fragile ceasefire the two sides reached last October.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Armed separatists attacked a security post at a gold mine in Central Papua, killing two people and prompting Indonesian forces to evacuate seventy-five workers, among them twenty-six Chinese nationals.</s>
<s>Military searches continue in the surrounding highlands.</s>
<s>The attack is the latest episode in a decades-long struggle for West Papuan independence that receives little sustained international attention.</s>
<break time="900ms"/>
<s>On the economy.</s>
<break time="400ms"/>
<s>The European Parliament approved a trade agreement with the Mercosur bloc by four hundred and eighty-three votes, attaching safeguards that allow Brussels to suspend tariff benefits if agricultural imports from South America rise by five percent.</s>
<s>Argentina backed the deal despite the caps, seeking new export markets as American tariffs limit its alternatives.</s>
<s>Ratification by individual member states is still required.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>South Korea's Samsung reclaimed the top position in global memory chip sales, posting nineteen point one billion dollars in quarterly revenue, a forty percent jump that displaced rival SK <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="ˈhaɪnɪks">Hynix</phoneme> from first place.</s>
<s>Legacy chip prices surged fifty percent in the final quarter of last year.</s>
<s>A state-backed Chinese manufacturer continues to undercut both companies with memory chips at half the market price.</s>
<break time="900ms"/>
<s>In science.</s>
<break time="400ms"/>
<s>An artificial intelligence system called DeepRare matched or outperformed physicians across nearly three thousand rare conditions in a study published in the journal Nature.</s>
<s>The system uses forty specialized tools and generates traceable reasoning that experts confirmed correct ninety-five percent of the time.</s>
<s>Three hundred million people globally live with rare diseases, typically spending more than five years without a correct diagnosis.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Rising atmospheric carbon dioxide is depleting nitrogen in Sweden's boreal forests, according to a Nature study of tree-ring records spanning nearly six decades.</s>
<s>As trees grow faster in a carbon-rich atmosphere, they outstrip the soil's ability to resupply nutrients, locking them in plant litter rather than returning them to the ground.</s>
<s>Climate models that count these northern forests as a growing carbon sink may significantly overestimate their capacity.</s>
<break time="900ms"/>
<s>In technology.</s>
<break time="400ms"/>
<s>A Nature study found that nearly five thousand users assigned to the social platform X's algorithmic feed shifted measurably rightward on political issues over seven weeks, compared with users on a chronological feed.</s>
<s>The shift persisted after users returned to chronological browsing, because the algorithm had already changed who they followed.</s>
<s>This research adds weight to longstanding concerns about how recommendation systems reshape political belief well beyond any single session online.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>A botnet built from millions of hijacked devices overwhelmed the Invisible Internet Project, a privacy network used by journalists, activists, and people in countries with censored internet access.</s>
<s>The botnet had lost its own command servers and rerouted its traffic through the network, outnumbering legitimate users thirty-nine to one.</s>
<s>Developers restored the network within six days, adding new protections against future attacks.</s>
<break time="1s"/>
<s>That's your briefing from <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="zʊhd">zuhd</phoneme> news.</s>
<break time="500ms"/>
<s>We're back in twelve hours.</s>
<break time="300ms"/>
<s><phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="ʔɪn ʃæːʔ ɑɫ.ɫɑːh">إن شاء الله</phoneme>.</s>
</speak>